============================================================================
VERDICT
============================================================================
[NUM] For any finite |V0| >~ 0.2 (either sign), EXACTLY ONE miniband
      becomes core-localized (weight -> q, splits off the spectrum); the
      remaining q-1 = 5 stay extended (weight ~ 1). Never 0, never 2.
[LIT] This matches the CdGM/spectral-flow count: one core level per unit
      winding per channel.
=> The counting mechanism 'vortex reserves one state per cell -> filling
   nu = (q-1)/q' is CONSISTENT in the model (F-Q1 survives). Remaining
   honest condition: in the [HYP-SC] weak-comb regime the reserved state
   is a statement about the UNDERLYING vortex (CdGM level bound in the
   full gap structure), not about the weak comb itself -- i.e. nu = 5/6
   is upgraded from bare assertion to a CdGM-counting hypothesis
   [HYP -> HYP+LIT], with the full BdG-on-vortex-lattice computation as
   the future closure step.
